{"title":"2012 CEMC Euclid Problems/Problem 1a","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2012 CEMC Euclid Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_1a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>John buys 10 bags of apples, each of which contains 20 apples. If he eats 8 apples a day, how many days will it take him to eat the 10 bags of apples?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_1a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since John has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> bags of apples and each has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> apples, he must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/9/5b950647b89e61f8535c938a8b9ce0705a209c90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10 \\times 20 = 200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"112\" height=\"15\" /> apples in total for all of the bags that he bought.\n</p><p>Thus, it will take him <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/7/4a7ece9f50f05e41cacee776a9f7344fd221e558.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{200}{8} = 25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"73\" height=\"37\" /> days to eat all of the apples.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017230359\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.010 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.014 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 22/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 78/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 722/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.660      1 2012_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_1\n100.00%    6.660      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36046:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017230359 and revision id 279732. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}